<title>NETHERLANDS: AMS Litho shares buoyed by new order.</title>
<headline>AMS Litho shares buoyed by new order.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The share price of semiconductor equipment maker ASM Lithography rose almost six percent in early trading after it announced it had won an order of more than $150 million.</p>
<p>The shares were trading at 133.60 guilders at 0750 GMT, up 6.80, after earlier reaching a year's high of 133.90.</p>
<p>The company said the order was won from Micron Technology, one of the world's largest makers of computer memory chips.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
